{"content":{"author":"/root/review_docs_accuracy","blocks":[{"text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_docs_accuracy\nPayload:\nAdversarial review found two blocking documentation issues and several smaller ones. No files edited.\n\n1. **Blocking — packaged README links will be broken.**  \n   [package.json:30](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/annals/package.json:30) allowlists `dist`, `README.md`, and `LICENSE`, but not `docs`. The README links to all three `docs/*.md` files at [README.md:42](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/annals/README.md:42) and [README.md:80](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/annals/README.md:80). Source-built tarballs and a future npm package will therefore contain a README whose documentation links resolve nowhere. Add `\"docs\"` to `files`, and ideally make `docs:check` validate package contents or run `npm pack --dry-run`.\n\n2. **Blocking — AGENTS recommends a command this package does not implement.**  \n   [AGENTS.md:49](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/annals/AGENTS.md:49) tells humans to run `annals review`, but the default CLI only implements `sync` and `transport-push` ([src/cli.ts:75](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/annals/src/cli.ts:75)). This is especially problematic because it is security-remediation guidance. Refer to the owning producer CLI’s review workflow, explicitly note that bare annals has no review command, or implement the missing CLI surface. The pre-existing scan guidance has the same mismatch at [src/store.ts:871](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/annals/src/store.ts:871).\n\n3. **High/conditional — development docs claim CI already exists.**  \n   [docs/development.md:64](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/annals/docs/development.md:64) says a workflow runs on PRs and `main` with `gitleaks`, but there is no `.github/workflows` file in this worktree. Fine only if the CI PR is merged first; otherwise make this future-tense or add the workflow in the same change.\n\n4. **Medium — “enriches” overstates deduplication behavior.**  \n   [docs/architecture.md:54](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/annals/docs/architecture.md:54) says a rescan under a newer producer version “enriches or deduplicates” the fact. The store does not merge provenance: same-anchor append discards the later copy, while cross-anchor reads select one deterministic representative. Say the identity remains stable and the copies deduplicate; do not imply metadata enrichment is persisted. The language at [README.md:131](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/annals/README.md:131) should likewise distinguish identity stability from storage merge semantics.\n\n5. **Medium — environment-redaction description is narrower than implementation.**  \n   [docs/configuration.md:54](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/annals/docs/configuration.md:54) says values come from “secret-shaped process variables.” `collectEnvValues()` actually takes every environment value of at least eight characters except an explicit routine-name allowlist and path-like values ([src/redact/config.ts:242](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/annals/src/redact/config.ts:242)). Replace with “eligible process variables” and state the actual exclusions.\n\n6. **Medium — practical README still omits the public CLI.**  \n   The new documentation contract requires CLI commands and flags in README ([AGENTS.md:21](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/annals/AGENTS.md:21)), but README has no CLI section. Document `annals sync [remote] [--all] [--no-scan]`, especially the scope and security implications of `--all` and `--no-scan`; label `transport-push` as the hook entrypoint.\n\n7. **Low — quick start assumes ESM without saying so.**  \n   [README.md:47](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/annals/README.md:47) uses static `import`, while the package is ESM-only ([package.json:5](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/annals/package.json:5)). A short note that the example assumes an ESM project would