{"content":{"blocks":[{"content":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\ninterface AllowlistFile {\n  fingerprints: string[];\n}\n\nfunction allowlistPath(repo: Ledger): string {\n  return join(repo.commonDir, repo.ns.stateDirName, \"allowlist.json\");\n}\n\n/**\n * The user-wide tier, next to the global config. A false positive is usually\n * a property of the *text* (a fixture, a doc example), not of the repo it was\n * captured in — the same span flagged here today gets flagged in the next\n * repo that reads the same file or quotes the same doc. Observed while\n * dogfooding: 2 of turnbridge's 4 outstanding fingerprints were already\n * human-approved in this namespace's per-repo allowlist, waiting to be\n * re-reviewed from scratch.\n */\nfunction globalAllowlistPath(repo: Ledger): string {\n  return join(homedir(), \".config\", repo.ns.userConfigDir, \"allowlist.json\");\n}\n\nasync function readAllowlistFile(path: string): Promise<string[]> {\n  try {\n    const raw = await readFile(path, \"utf8\");\n    const parsed = JSON.parse(raw) as AllowlistFile;\n    return Array.isArray(parsed.fingerprints) ? parsed.fingerprints : [];\n  } catch {\n    // Missing or malformed allowlist: treat as empty rather than failing the scan/sync.\n    return [];\n  }\n}\n\n/**\n * Union of every allowlist tier: the repo-local file under `.git/`, the\n * user-global file under `~/.config/<namespace>/`, and — when the caller passes\n * config — `scan.allowFingerprints` from the repo/global config, the\n * only tier that travels with a clone. All rebuildable-if-lost state, never\n * the record of truth; a fingerprint in any tier suppresses the finding.\n */\nexport async function loadAllowlist(repo: Ledger, config?: AnnalsConfig): Promise<Set<string>> {\n  const [local, global] = await Promise.all([\n    readAllowlistFile(allowlistPath(repo)),\n    readAllowlistFile(globalAllowlistPath(repo)),\n  ]);\n# annals\n\nAppend-only records anchored to git commits: typed, linkable, redacted on\nwrite, synced through git notes. annals is the storage layer extracted from\n[conversation-ledger](https://github.com/evintunador/conversation-ledger)\n(cledger), which now sits on top of it as one vocabulary among several.\n\nA record (\"event\") is a JSON object stored one-per-line in a git note attached\nto the commit that was `HEAD` when it happened. Because storage is git notes\nunder a dedicated ref, records travel with `git push`/`git fetch` (a pre-push\nhook and a fetch refspec are installed on first append), survive clones, and\nscope naturally: \"records reachable from this branch\" is a ref walk.\n\nannals is intentionally pre-release and is not published to npm yet. Its\nenvelope and namespace contracts are being exercised by downstream producers\nbefore a public release.\n\n## Install from source\n\nUse Node.js 20 or newer. For a reproducible downstream install, build a\ntarball from a known commit:\n\n```sh\ngit clone https://github.com/evintunador/annals.git\ncd annals\nnpm ci\nnpm test\nnpm pack\n\ncd /path/to/your-project\nnpm install /path/to/annals/annals-0.1.0.tgz\n```\n\nDuring active development, `npm install /path/to/annals` is convenient. A\nGitHub dependency also works, but pin a full commit SHA while the API is\npre-release:\n\n```sh\nnpm install github:evintunador/annals#FULL_COMMIT_SHA\n```\n\nSee [development and source installation](docs/development.md) for the full\nworkflow.\n\n## Library quick start\n\n```js\nimport { appendEvents, findRepo, openLedger, readEvents } from \"annals\";\n\nconst repo = await findRepo(process.cwd());\nif (!repo) throw new Error(\"run this inside a git repository\");\n\nconst ledger = openLedger(repo);\nawait appendEvents(ledger, [{\n  kind: \"example.created\",\n  occurred_at: new Date().toISOString(),\n  producer: { tool: \"example-app\", version: \"0.1.0\" },\n  content: { message: \"hello\" },\n}]);\n\nconst events = await readEvents(ledger); // records reachable from HEAD\n```\n\nFor an independent producer namespace, pass a partial namespace configuration\nto `openLedger()`:\n\n```js\nconst ledger = openLedger(repo, {\n  name: \"example-app\",\n  configFile: \".example-app.json\",\n  userConfigDir: \"example-app\",\n  cliName: \"example-app\",\n});\n```\n\nA custom namespace should provide a `hookInvocation` or expose a CLI named by\n`cliName` with a compatible `transport-push` command. Otherwise, call `sync()`\nthrough the library instead of relying on the pre-push hook.\n\n## Documentation\n\n- [Architecture](docs/architecture.md) covers identity, storage, reachability,\n  transport, and the privacy model.\n- [Configuration](docs/configuration.md) lists every setting and its default.\n- [Development and source installation](docs/development.md) covers local\n  builds, checks, downstream consumption, and release status.\n\n## What annals owns, and what it refuses to own\n\nannals owns **facts about records**: identity, dedup, ordering, links,\n\nTo install directly from GitHub, pin a full commit SHA rather than `main`:\n\n```sh\nnpm install github:evintunador/annals#FULL_COMMIT_SHA\n```\n\nThe repository's `prepare` script builds `dist` during that installation.\nCommit pinning matters because the package is intentionally pre-release and\ndoes not yet promise a stable public API.\n\n## Project checks\n\n- `npm run build` compiles TypeScript and makes the CLI executable.\n- `npm run docs:check` verifies internal documentation links and documentation\n  contract sentinels.\n- `npm test` builds and runs the complete test suite.\n- `npm pack --dry-run` previews the eventual published package.\n\n## Release status\n\nThe package metadata is present to exercise the real package shape, but there\nis deliberately no npm publication, git tag, or GitHub release yet. A future\nrelease should only happen after downstream vocabularies have exercised the\nnamespace, identity, and migration contracts.\nBefore committing, run:\n\n```sh\nnpm run docs:check\nnpm test\n```\n\n`npm run docs:check` enforces the mechanical portion of this contract. Review\nstill needs to verify that prose describes the behavior and tradeoffs rather\nthan merely naming the current symbols. This file makes that responsibility\nvisible to coding agents at the start of a task; automated checks prevent the\nobjective parts from silently drifting.\n\n## Secret-shaped fixtures\n\nNever write a format-valid fake credential whole in source, documentation,\nchat, or a commit message. Store detector-shaped values split as\n`secret_parts` in `src/test/fixtures/secret-corpus.json` and reassemble them in\nthe test. For keyword-shaped examples, include an uppercase marker such as\n`FAKE`, `EXAMPLE`, `PLACEHOLDER`, `DUMMY`, `NOTREAL`, or `TESTONLY` in the\nvalue. See `CLAUDE.md` for the full rationale and review procedure.\n\nIf a push-time scan reports a finding, stop and ask a human to run\n`annals review` in a plain terminal. Do not print or inspect the flagged\ncontent in an agent session.\n","type":"input_text"}],"tool_use_id":"call_JDyO1v1AOBa3MlutdAn7nF6D","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"tool_result"},"context":{"branch":"docs-standalone-guides","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/annals","head":"9d339893b896ee215d81fdc90b0191a1ef869ebf","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/annals.git"},"id":"ev2-8f8ddaaf1d815bb517373879db1a675d19b353190a77886914e576187e58d9e1","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"type":"system"},"model":"gpt-5.6-sol","provider":"openai","session_id":"01a0d131-8563-7453-ae36-468e6c8930b5","source":"codex","source_version":"0.156.1"},"occurred_at":"2026-09-25T00:24:15.906Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.26.0"},"raw":{"data":{"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000},"ordinal":288,"payload":{"call_id":"call_JDyO1v1AOBa3MlutdAn7nF6D","id":"ctco_01a0d5f2-d322-7140-94e9-98bf59946396","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_tim